 <&_ if (fragment.testingSection) { -&>
 ### Svelte tests

 Unit tests are run by [Jest][]. They're located alongside components and can be run with:

 ```
 npm test
 ```

 UI end-to-end tests are powered by [Cypress][]. They're located under cypress directory and can be run by starting Spring Boot in one terminal (`./mvnw spring-boot:run`) and running the tests (`npm run e2e`) in a second one.

<%_ if (playwright) { _%>
 ### Playwright end-to-end tests

 Playwright tests are in `playwright/`. Install Chromium once with `npx playwright install chromium` (use `--with-deps` on Linux CI), start the application, then run `npm run e2e:playwright`.

 The default application URL is `http://localhost:8080`. Set `PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL` to test another running instance, such as the Vite server on port 9000. Set `ADMIN_USERNAME` and `ADMIN_PASSWORD` when the default admin account has changed. OAuth2 tests use the generated Keycloak login page; adapt `playwright/support/auth.js` for another identity provider.

 Regular-user navigation tests use `USER_USERNAME` and `USER_PASSWORD`, both defaulting to `user`.

 `npm run e2e:playwright:ui` opens Playwright's interactive runner. Tests use isolated browser contexts, block service workers and retain traces and screenshots on failure. Run them against a development or test database: tests create and delete records and exercise account settings. Cypress and its existing `e2e` commands remain available.
<%_ } _%>

